create-and-append.bodyMarkdown:
When data contains several records, create real DOM elements instead of building one large HTML string.

```js
const list = document.querySelector("#event-list");
const item = document.createElement("li");

item.textContent = "Jazz Night - Music Center";
list.append(item);
```

Step by step:

1. `list` refers to the existing list.
2. `createElement("li")` creates a new list item.
3. `textContent` gives it readable content.
4. `append` inserts it into the page.

You do not need `innerHTML` or `map(...).join(...)` to render beginner projects.
